# Type assumptions and their persistence/forgetting
assume a byte is unsigned
what is the range of x for a byte x?
assume bytes are signed
what is the range of x plus 1 for a byte x?
does x times x overflow for a 16-bit unsigned x?
what is the range of x divided by 2 for a 32-bit signed x?
what is the range of n for an integer n between 1 and 12?
what is the range of 2 to the n for n between 0 and 10?
forget everything
what is the range of x for a byte x?
assume int means i32
does x plus 1 overflow for an int x?
assume int means unbounded
does x plus 1 overflow for an int x?
